    "q-40661": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40661",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the subspace spanned by $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nIn our case, $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={14}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-40661-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}]",
