    "q-95346": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95346",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Which of the following are orthogonal projection matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that $Q$ is an orthogonal projection matrix if and only if ${Q}^{2}=Q$ and ${Q}^{T}=Q.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is an orthogonal projection matrix. Indeed,\n${A}^{T}=A$\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5} & -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{T}\\ne B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* an orthogonal projection matrix. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{T}\\ne C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95346-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$B$ only",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"49\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D435 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95346-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$A$ only",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"50\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D434 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95346-c",
